  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "tools: Avoid race condition with pngcrush output name",
  "description": "The shell script version of this would automatically substitute the\nprocess ID for $$ but that doesn't happen with Python, so it's possible\nthat when these are run in parallel that two PNGs in the same directory\nmight have the same temp output file. Add a pngcrush suffix to the\ninput filename for the temp file to avoid that.\n\nFix #19950\n\nThe issue with version 1.8.0 (released in 2016) not having \"-noforce\" and\nforcing by default probably isn't worth trying to address. Versions\nbefore 1.8.0 will ignore \"-noforce\" but also don't force by default so\nit's no problem.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
